  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/xhtml.html#parsing-xhtml-documents\n\n>  the public identifiers given in the following list all correspond to the URL given by this link\n\nThe DTD linked from there includes the following entity definitions:\n\n```\n<!ENTITY amp \"&#x26;\">\n[...]\n<!ENTITY lt \"&#x3C;\">\n```\n\nThese definitions violate XML specification, [section 4.6](http://www.w3.org/TR/xml/#sec-predefined-ent), which requires the replacement text for these entities to be character references to the corresponding characters rather than the characters themselves.\n\nAlso, the replacement text for `AMP`, `LT` and `nvlt` entities contains invalid markup, which makes these entities unusable. Probably these should also be replaced with character references.\n",
